WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.200
On July 17th, Apple overtook NVIDIA to&nbsp;
become the most valuable company on Earth.&nbsp;

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.480
And they did, by essentially ignoring AI.&nbsp;

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:10.954
So… how?
For years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.954 --> 00:00:14.040
Apple was mocked for being “behind” on AI.
They spend about 2% of sales on AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:18.920
while the Hyperscalers spend 39%.
They also became the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:25.400
company to pass $5 trillion in market cap.
How is Apple winning, by refusing to build AI?&nbsp;

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:38.280
This is how Apple won the AI race… by ignoring it.
Before vs now&nbsp;

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:45.960
This might not sound that surprising.&nbsp;
“Oh Apple is #1 again, what else is new”&nbsp;

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:50.680
But just a few years or even months&nbsp;
ago, you wouldn’t think they’d be here.&nbsp;

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:57.240
From early 2022, all the way to early 2026,&nbsp;
Apple had a bit of a mixed performance.&nbsp;

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:03.480
A big one was last year, where Apple&nbsp;
fell almost 19% between April and May.&nbsp;

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.120
Not only were there lawsuits and tariffs on&nbsp;
Chinese components that would now affect Apple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:14.600
a big focus was on their lacklustre AI products.
“Siri’s initial promise was to revolutionize user&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:20.040
interaction with Apple devices through voice&nbsp;
commands and intelligent assistance. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.120
users have frequently reported frustrations&nbsp;
with Siri’s limited understanding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.360
lack of contextual awareness, and&nbsp;
inability to perform complex tasks.”&nbsp;

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.760
The new “AI powered” Siri which was supposed&nbsp;
to be integrated into your mail, calendar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:38.040
messages, was delayed, had hundreds of&nbsp;
bugs, and general underwhelming reception.&nbsp;

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:43.080
So, Apple postponed it indefinitely.
We also got Apple Intelligence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.400
revealed at WWDC24.
But as it rolled out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.080
also came more problems.
More delays, more features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:57.160
postponed, general user dissatisfaction.
Despite this, Apple overpromised what the AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:02.520
could actually do, and promoted features that&nbsp;
Apple Intelligence couldn’t even perform yet.&nbsp;

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.640
So they discontinued a major TV ad&nbsp;
for the new AI Siri, among others.&nbsp;

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:13.480
The features were then promoted as an&nbsp;
iPhone 17 feature… instead of the iPhone 16.&nbsp;

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.960
What added fuel to this AI dumpster&nbsp;
fire, was the leadership collapse.&nbsp;

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:22.280
AI chief John Giannandrea announced&nbsp;
his retirement in December 2025,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:27.080
over concerns about product direction.
Siri was moved under Mike Rockwell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:31.320
who launched the Vision Pro. And&nbsp;
we all know how well that one went.&nbsp;

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:37.480
Then Apple decided to change course.
Apple’s main AI partner, was ChatGPT.&nbsp;

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:42.040
Makes sense, for a while they&nbsp;
seemed like the only AI partner.&nbsp;

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:47.400
But that soon fell apart, and Apple&nbsp;
recently sued OpenAI for trade secret theft.&nbsp;

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.000
They instead went with Google&nbsp;
Gemini. A better choice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:58.040
but it was also seen as a bit of a self-own.
“The 1.2 trillion parameters of Google’s AI make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:04.760
Apple’s 150 million parameters for the cloud-based&nbsp;
version of Apple Intelligence almost embarrassing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:10.600
and while I have little doubt that Apple, with the&nbsp;
help of Google, will get AI on its devices right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:15.480
it’s hard not to ignore the mess that the&nbsp;
Cupertino-based tech giant has found itself in.”&nbsp;

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:22.760
Plus, Google already pays Apple an estimated $20B&nbsp;
a year to be the default Safari search engine.&nbsp;

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.520
Apple was now paying Google back.
In a way, it seemed like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:30.520
Apple was going backwards.
Falling behind the next boom.

